abstract: >-
  FrameAssembly is a domain-specific language (DSL), optimizing compiler, and PCAP-to-.frasm
  decompiler written in Rust that compiles strict-lowercase network packet code (.frasm)
  into deterministic, wire-valid classic libpcap (.pcap) and PCAPNG (.pcapng) packet captures—and
  decompiles .pcap / .pcapng captures back into canonical .frasm code (bidirectional .frasm <->
  .pcap/.pcapng compilation and decompilation)—across 81 native Layer 2 through Layer 7 protocols
  with dual-stack IPv4/IPv6 flows, stateful 4-tuple
  TCP sequence progression, and cryptographic SNMPv3 USM authentication and privacy.
